/--
Successful imported primitive-call `evalValues` preserves the exact visible
varstore domain when argument evaluation does and the primitive itself restores
the caller varstore.

This deliberately keeps the operation-specific proof as the small
`hPrimStore` premise, so recursive bridge cases can use one common adapter
instead of unfolding `primCall` for every primitive expression.
