/--
Checked regular exact-domain sequence boundary that also preserves the entry
fresh-coverage invariant.

This is the checked facade needed for bracketed-block list heads: the nested
body may introduce and then scope-clean source locals semantically, but the
outer list lowerer only needs to know that the generated fresh state still
covers the outer entry layout before compiling the tail.
-/
def CheckedRegularSeqLoweringSoundWhenFreshAtCompileFuelExactDomain
    (cfg : StateRelConfig) (layout layoutAfter : List Name)
    (prim : Objects.Source.PrimitiveSemantics)
    (program : Functions.Program) (ctx : Functions.Source.Ctx)
    (sourceFuel targetFuel compileFuel : Nat)
    (sourceStmts : List AstStmt) (codeOverride : Option AstContract) :
    Prop :=
  ∀ {freshState freshState' lowerBlock},
    FreshCoversLayout layout freshState →
    Stmt.List.toBlockFuel? compileFuel freshState sourceStmts =
      some (lowerBlock, freshState') →
    FreshCoversLayout layout freshState' ∧
      SourceRegularSeqSoundAtFuelExactDomain cfg layout layoutAfter prim
        program ctx sourceFuel targetFuel sourceStmts codeOverride lowerBlock

/--
Names-aware regular exact-domain sequence target.

`layout` is the currently visible source scope. `reserved` is the surrounding
source-name set that the concrete fresh state is known to contain before
lowering, even when those names are not visible yet. This is the missing
invariant for top-level `let`: a declaration name is fresh for the current
layout but must already be marked used by the contract-level fresh generator.
-/
