/--
Accepted-program recursive bridge boundary.

This is the top-down induction target for the actual final theorem.  Compared
with `ProgramRecursiveSourceBridgeWhenUpToAtExactCompatNames`, each statement
or block field is guarded by the source-language facts that make the imported
Yul construct part of the accepted program: `Safe`, source lexical scoping,
`ControlFlow`, and `UserCallArity`.

That matters because the final compiler theorem should not try to prove the
bridge for arbitrary invalid/unsupported Yul fragments such as code-image
primitives before the code-image semantics exists.  Those constructs are ruled
out at the accepted-program boundary.
-/
