/--
Checked statement soundness for source shapes that the compiler refuses to
lower.

This keeps the accepted-frontier dispatcher honest: accepted source syntax may
contain shapes that are semantically meaningful but outside this checked
lowering path, such as a multi-target non-call initializer.  At the checked
lowering boundary those branches are impossible rather than semantic
obligations.
